course: dictionary
lesson: 5115
title: Intolerant: three meanings from context
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must use context to find the right one. Read the words around the word and ask: which meaning fits here? «Grown-ups who get tummy trouble from milk are called lactose intolerant.» The clue is tummy trouble, so intolerant here means your body cannot digest a food well.
explain: Intolerant can also describe people. It means not willing to accept people whose ideas, beliefs or ways are different from yours. This is an unkind, closed-minded attitude. Check it by swapping in your meaning: does «intolerant of other people's beliefs» still make sense? It does, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: The third meaning is unable to put up with something, like noise or cold. «He is intolerant of loud noise» means loud noise bothers him so much that he cannot bear it. The phrase intolerant of is your clue: it is followed by the thing that is hard to put up with.
fact: Intolerant means not willing to accept people whose ideas, beliefs or ways are different from yours.
fact: «Lactose intolerant» means your body cannot digest milk well, and it can make your tummy hurt.
fact: Intolerant of something means unable to put up with it, like noise or cold.
fact: The noun is intolerance, and the phrases are «intolerant of» and «be intolerant to».
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word to use: look at the words that come after it and around it.
exercise: «Grown-ups who get tummy trouble from milk are called lactose intolerant.» What does intolerant mean here? | They are very tired after a long day | They never accept other people's ideas | They love milk so much they cannot stop drinking it | *Their bodies cannot digest milk well
exercise: Mia says, «He is intolerant of loud noise, so he covers his ears at the fireworks.» What does intolerant of loud noise mean? | Is deaf and cannot hear anything | Enjoys loud noise and music very much | *Unable to put up with loud noise | Shouts louder than everyone else
exercise: «The club's rules were intolerant, refusing anyone whose beliefs were different.» What does intolerant mean in this sentence? | Tall and strong enough to lift heavy bags | Very kind and welcoming to everyone | *Not willing to accept people who are different | Happy to share its food with new people
test: «Sam is intolerant of gluten, so bread makes his tummy hurt.» What does intolerant mean here? | Likes to be on his own | *Cannot digest a food well | Loves bread more than anything | Forgets what he has eaten
test: What does intolerance mean when it is about people? | Liking to read many books | Being very friendly to everyone you meet | Eating too much bread | *Not being willing to accept people whose ideas are different
exam: Which phrase means unable to put up with cold or noise? | agree with | *intolerant of | be happy to | digest well
